<h3 id="what-it-does">What it does</h3>

<p>Select one or more Markdown notes, then choose <strong>Publish to Marked Share</strong> from DEVONthink&rsquo;s script menu or the contextual menu. Text records named <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">.md</code> or <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">.markdown</code> count too. Everything else in the selection is skipped.</p>

<p>The first run opens Connect an app in your browser. Sign in there. The script never asks for your Marked Share password. The keys come back to a helper in your Applications folder and land in the Keychain. Hold Shift the next time you run it if you need to connect again.</p>

<p>One dialog asks for a folder. Leave it blank and new notes go to the library root. Type a folder that already exists and the notes are filed there. The share links are copied to the clipboard, and each record keeps the link in custom metadata so the record&rsquo;s own URL stays put.</p>

<h3 id="installing">Installing</h3>

<p>Open the package. It installs for the current user and does not ask for an administrator password. It adds the script to DEVONthink&rsquo;s menus and drops the login helper in <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">~/Applications</code>. The first time it runs, allow it to control DEVONthink when macOS asks.</p>

